nces where on domestic issues  he has been  right in line with the present  democratic philosophy of of government  control and subsidy and regulation and  so forth which would be contrary  to republican philosophy at the moment  no question that he's expressed some  views particularly in the international  scene regarding americanism and  patriotism and so forth that i'm sure a  few people uh disagree with what about  his position on racist problems well  he seems to have avoided that subject  pretty well i haven't uh heard too many  statements without that i've heard  everything he says or even paid too much  attention to what it but i haven't heard  uh that much has been said that he's  well is what i mean against integration  to make a specific point  well i happen to be one who believes in  first of all i'm i am incapable of  feeling prejudice myself  i do not believe in discrimination  and i  certainly believe in equality of  opportunity for all people  and i believe that the answer to the  problem will come  someday when  all of us in america will stop using  just as we've stopped using the labels  in our party we'll stop hyphenating  ourselves and using a word in front of  american without with a hyphen let's  let's go back to these labels governor  that you object to but most people in  this country  employ in common talk  liberal and conservative  senator kiekel lost to max rafferty and  there doesn't seem much argument  within the republican party that kiko  represented the moderate or liberal wing  and rafferty the conservative perhaps  the right wing what do you make of that  well i recall  during the campaign hearing both of them  comparing  one the contender comparing his views  and the other comparing his vote record  with the voting record of senator george  murphy  and  they came out about even  with the support of the things that  george murphy had stood for  now  i think the the kiko rafferty campaign  there are a lot number of factors first  of 