licans have to nominate  a nominee  if the people  do not know  where the republicans stand if they  don't talk about one another how are  they supposed to decide  well in california 1966 we waged a  primary in which we campaigned our views  and what we would do as opposed to those  of the incumbent democratic  administration and the people made the  decision on who they thought would be  the best replacement for that  administration this does not mean that  you take on the other you state your  case you run against the opposition you  know this is a tryout  for who's going to run in the big race  against the other school and i've  likened it to a  track meet if on wednesday afternoon the  kids go out on the track to do a hundred  yards to determine who's gonna run on  saturday against the other school in the  big track meet  you've tried to find out who's the  fastest you don't go down the track  spiking each other  to see who can be the only survivor yeah  but that's a different game governor  that's not politics no i don't think  it's a different game what are we  interested in we are interested in the  views of the republican candidates  and what they would offer and what they  would propose  in contrast  to the leadership that we now have in  washington  and  thus there's no need  to point a finger at any other  republican candidate you state your case  what you would  it's always happened in every campaign  particularly in primaries and i'm sure  it happened in the 66 primary between  you and george christopher well  no i would ask you to go back and find  one  word that i ever said about him  but it takes two you know he said a  great many things well um  uh  whether that had anything to do with the  result or not um  people made a decision governor would  you say there's a fundamental difference  between your position on vietnam and  that of nelson rockefeller  i can't say that i'm a complete  authority on his position i used this  just as an example a momen