licans have to nominate  a nominee  if the people  do not know  where the republicans stand if they  don't talk about one another how are  they supposed to decide  well in california 1966 we waged a  primary in which we campaigned our views  and what we would do as opposed to those  of the incumbent democratic  administration and the people made the  decision on who they thought would be  the best replacement for that  administration this does not mean that  you take on the other you state your  case you run against the opposition you  know this is a tryout  for who's going to run in the big race  against the other school and i've  likened it to a  track meet if on wednesday afternoon the  kids go out on the track to do a hundred  yards to determine who's gonna run on  saturday against the other school in the  big track meet  you've tried to find out who's the  fastest you don't go down the track  spiking each other  to see who can be the only survivor yeah  but that's a different game governor  that's not politics no i don't think  it's a different game what are we  interested in we are interested in the  views of the republican candidates  and what they would offer and what they  would propose  in contrast  to the leadership that we now have in  washington  and  thus there's no need  to point a finger at any other  republican candidate you state your case  what you would  it's always happened in every campaign  particularly in primaries and i'm sure  it happened in the 66 primary between  you and george christopher well  no i would ask you to go back and find  one  word that i ever said about him  but it takes two you know he said a  great many things well um  uh  whether that had anything to do with the  result or not um  people made a decision governor would  you say there's a fundamental difference  between your position on vietnam and  that of nelson rockefeller  i can't say that i'm a complete  authority on his position i used this  just as an example a moment ago and  incidentally let me correct one  if i gave an impression there  that this meant that i was supposed to  be favoring one over the other no you  asked a question i honestly tried to  answer it but at the same time  in governor's conferences  governor rockefeller and i have been in  great agreement on many times across the  table on issues that were confronting us  the  i know that he is is  has announced  whether he has stated it already or not  a position or that he's going to explain  a position on vietnam but it has been my  when i said there was a that i perhaps  was closer on that one used looking for  an example  i think that what i was actually trying  to say was that both richard nixon and i  have over the period of the past year  spoken out against the limited war  concept  against a win policy and against the  need to be there  now  and against the need to be there you  mean you're willing to lose against the  no no no against did i say win against  the no no the no win policy  uh  it's been my impression that uh  perhaps nelson is placing a  little more faith in the negotiations  or in some kind of compromise settlement  than i find myself able to you have no  faith in that prospect of paris oh i i  can hope for peace  but i don't hope for the kind of peace  that would result in say  a concession that would allow the viet  cong to be a a part of the  south vietnamese government i think this  would be about the same as the united  states government taking the casa nostra  in his partners governor if we can if we  can move to a different topic  the day after senator kennedy died or  perhaps it was the day he died  you blamed demagogic and irresponsible  leaders in and out of office you said  that their words had fed this attitude  of lawlessness in our society  and as i recall after that news  conference in sacramento you refuse to  identify any of them or you fail to  identify them can you tell us now what  kind of people do you have in mind what  what are their names well bill let me  straight one thing out i didn't say  demagogic leaders i said demagogic  statements by people in and out of  public office  now a demagogic statement can be  deliberate it can also simply be  carelessness on the part of the  individual who  didn't intend to be a demagogue but  you can go back one of the reasons for  not naming an individual  is to try and pick out and name one  would be unfair unless you were going to  compile a list of all of them and their  statements and say here all of these  statements we think have contributed to  this atmosphere but we have had  statements first specifically  do you have senator did you have senator  robert kennedy's statements in mind his  own statement i can only tell you that  robert kennedy in the last several weeks  in california  has actually been campaigning  on a basis of  healing the wounds restoring law and  order stopping the violence in our  countries  i was talking about i wasn't talking  about individuals i was talking about  statements and i would repeat and  practice some of those statements all  right some of them might have been  attributed to him but statements such as  someone saying that if he lived in a  slum he too would join a rebellion or  could not you would you're pretty right  is that what you're talking about uh  this is the kind of statement i'm  talking about i'm talking about  statements made several years ago of a  statement that perhaps a jail record  would be a mark of honor  in this country  with regard to being arrested for  demonstrations and so forth i'm talking  about any statement of the kind that  encourages riots now these could  encompass a great many commencement  speakers of the last week or so who have  appeared on a number of campuses and  they come from a number of lines of  activity including academic including  the judicial  and public figures who have talked about  encouraging  uh supposedly  just dissent but encouraging the the  type 