e going to be  disillusioned that were deluded into  believing  that this could result in some immediate  answer to their problem now again you  get back to dissent and what is needed  in this country  there are great many voices have been  heard one of them was the late senator  robert kennedy's  saying virtually the same things that  i've been saying in california as a  matter of fact in california he was  advocating what we are doing in  california a program to provide jobs to  the poor to the minority  element and the  here in other words was a place  proper leaders of the poor should be  telling them  support those people today who are  advocating a change in the programs that  are a failure but governor even before  the horror of the ambassador hotel  robert kennedy also spoke for tougher  gun control laws and you have said we  probably have the best laws in the  nation in california now we do  you think we generally yes we do  gentlemen i really regret our time is up  thank you very much governor reagan for  being here to face the nation  a word about next week's guest in a  moment  today on face the nation governor ronald  reagan of california was interviewed by  cbs news correspondent bill stout paul  hope of the washington star cbs news  correspondent martin negronski led the  questioning  next week senator thomas dodd of  connecticut leader in the fight for a  strong gun control bill  and harold glassen president of the  national rifle association which is  fighting additional gun control  legislation will  face the nation  up next on real america we continue our  look back at the 1960
 

